        "thinking": "Now I have the full picture. The `members` and `invites` endpoints are truly missing and need to be implemented. The earlier 501s the user saw were correct.\n\nLet me now build a comprehensive implementation. Looking at the audit results, the routes that the UI actually needs are:\n\n**Most critical for UI functionality:**\n1. `GET /api/companies/:id/members` — Access page\n2. `PATCH /api/companies/:id/members/:id` — Update member\n3. `PATCH /api/companies/:id/members/:id/role-and-grants` — Update role\n\n\n4. `POST /api/companies/:id/members/:id/archive` — Archive member\n5. `PATCH /api/companies/:id/members/:id/permissions` — Update permissions\n6. `GET /api/companies/:id/invites` — Invites page\n7. `POST /api/companies/:id/invites` — Create invite\n8. `POST /api/invites/:inviteId/revoke` — Revoke invite\n9. `GET /api/companies/:id/skills/:skillId` — Skill detail\n10. `DELETE /api/companies/:id/skills/:skillId` — Delete skill\n11. `POST /api/companies/:id/join-requests/:id/approve` — Approve join request\n12. `POST /api/companies/:id/join-requests/:id/reject` — Reject join request\n\nFor CLI authentication, I need to add routes for challenge-based auth flow, plus endpoints to retrieve invite details and accept invites via token. Rather than rewriting each handler from scratch, I should create an adapter that bridges to the existing Express handler code, which relies on `req.actor` for access control checks.\n\nThe most practical solution is to build a fake Express request/response wrapper that lets me call the original handlers directly in the Cloudflare context. I'd construct a request object with the necessary params, query, body, and resolved actor, then capture the response. But that's essentially reimplementing Express routing, which feels inefficient.\n\nA cleaner approach: study the actual route implementations in `access.ts`, understand what each one does, then implement them as Hono handlers using the server's existing helper functions directly. It's more upfront work, but the result will be more maintainable and properly typed.\n\nLooking at the key routes I need to port over, like the company members and invites endpoints, they're mostly straightforward database queries that I can call directly. Let me focus on the read-only endpoints that the UI actually depends on.",
        "type": "thinking"
      }
